<section id="terms-of-service-en" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="text-sm mb-10">Last updated: September 25, 2026</p>

  <%!-- 1 --%>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">1. Purpose</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed mb-2">
      These terms of service (the "Terms") set out the rules for accessing and using the Teachercoop website,
      available at https://www.teachercoop.org (the "Site").
    </p>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">
      The Site is a personal, non-commercial project published by a private individual (see the <a
        href={~p"/legal-mentions"}
        class="underline"
      >legal mentions</a>). It allows teachers to search, view, download and share teaching resources.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%!-- 2 --%>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">2. Acceptance of the Terms</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">
      Creating an account implies full acceptance of these Terms. If you do not accept them, you must not create
      an account or use the features reserved for registered users.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%!-- 3 --%>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">3. Access to the Site and Free Use</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">
      Access to the Site and account creation are free of charge. Internet access and equipment costs remain
      the responsibility of the user.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%!-- 4 --%>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">4. Creating and Using Your Account</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed mb-2">
      To create an account, you must provide a valid email address that you own. You log in with a link sent
      to this address or, if you have set one, with a password.
    </p>
    <p class="leading-relaxed mb-2">You agree to:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
      <li>provide an accurate email address and keep it up to date;</li>
      <li>
        keep your mailbox secure and your password confidential, as they give access to your account;
      </li>
      <li>not create an account on behalf of someone else or use another user's account;</li>
      <li>
        report any unauthorized use of your account without delay to <a
          href="mailto:contact@teachercoop.org"
          class="underline"
        >contact@teachercoop.org</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <%!-- 5 --%>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">5. Rules of Use</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed mb-2">By using the Site, you agree not to:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
      <li>use the Site for illegal purposes or in breach of these Terms;</li>
      <li>
        attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Site, its servers or other users' accounts;
      </li>
      <li>
        disrupt the operation of the Site (mass requests, bots, introducing malicious code, etc.);
      </li>
      <li>collect information about other users.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <%!-- 6 --%>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">6. Account Suspension and Deletion</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed mb-2">
      You can delete your account at any time by writing to <a
        href="mailto:contact@teachercoop.org"
        class="underline"
      >contact@teachercoop.org</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="leading-relaxed mb-2">
      If you breach these Terms, the publisher may suspend or delete your account after informing you by email,
      except in an emergency or in case of a serious threat to the security of the Site.
    </p>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">
      Accounts inactive for 3 years are automatically deleted, in accordance with the <a
        href={~p"/privacy-policy"}
        class="underline"
      >privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%!-- 7 --%>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">7. Availability of the Site</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">
      As the Site is a personal project, the publisher strives to keep it available but does not guarantee
      continuous availability. The publisher may interrupt the Site, in particular for maintenance, modify it or
      shut it down at any time. If the Site is permanently closed, users will be informed by email within a
      reasonable time, and their data will be deleted.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%!-- 8 --%>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">8. Intellectual Property</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed mb-2">
      The source code of the Site is free software distributed under the AGPL-3.0 license (see the <a
        href={~p"/legal-mentions"}
        class="underline"
      >legal mentions</a>). Documents published by users remain the property of their authors.
    </p>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">
      Unless otherwise stated, the other elements of the Site (texts, images, logo) are the property of the
      publisher. Any reproduction or reuse without prior authorization is prohibited.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%!-- 9 --%>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">9. Liability</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">
      The Site is provided free of charge, as is. To the extent permitted by law, the publisher cannot be held
      liable for interruptions of the Site, data loss or indirect damages related to its use. Users are
      responsible for how they use the Site and their account.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%!-- 10 --%>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">10. Personal Data</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">
      The processing of your personal data is described in the <a
        href={~p"/privacy-policy"}
        class="underline"
      >privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%!-- 11 --%>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">11. Changes to the Terms</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">
      The publisher may modify these Terms. In case of a significant change, users will be informed by email or
      on the Site before it takes effect. Continuing to use the Site after that date constitutes acceptance of
      the new Terms.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%!-- 12 --%>
  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">12. Governing Law and Disputes</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed mb-2">
      These Terms are governed by French law.
    </p>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">
      In case of a dispute, you can contact the publisher at
      <a
        href="mailto:contact@teachercoop.org"
        class="underline"
      >contact@teachercoop.org</a>
      to seek an amicable solution. Failing that, the dispute will be brought
      before the competent French courts.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
